{"term":"custom","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:91e63eb37752fc6d80","definition":"Frequent repetition of the same behavior; way of behavior common to many; ordinary manner; habitual practice; method of doing, living or behaving.","example":"Much forbidden by elder custom is accepted today.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["fashion","folkway","habit","practice","usage","wone","wont"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["custom and practice","custom-built","custom house","customless","grow a custom","heir by custom","suit custom","take one's custom elsewhere","Ulster custom"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/custom#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:2209c79e5ee6ee845f","definition":"Habitual buying of goods from one same vendor.","example":"Thank you for your custom.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["fashion","folkway","habit","practice","usage","wone","wont"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["custom and practice","custom-built","custom house","customless","grow a custom","heir by custom","suit custom","take one's custom elsewhere","Ulster custom"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/custom#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:ede5af4633e402eba3","definition":"Long-established practice, considered as unwritten law, and resting for authority on long consent. Compare prescription.","example":"The distinction between custom and usage it that usage is a fact and custom is a law. There can be usage without custom, but not custom without usage.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["usage"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["custom and practice","custom-built","custom house","customless","grow a custom","heir by custom","suit custom","take one's custom elsewhere","Ulster custom"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/custom#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:23c1981af0c2cf01dc","definition":"Traditional beliefs or rituals.","example":"The Ancient Egyptian culture had many distinctive and interesting beliefs and customs; one custom was the mummification of the dead.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["fashion","folkway","habit","practice","usage","wone","wont"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["custom and practice","custom-built","custom house","customless","grow a custom","heir by custom","suit custom","take one's custom elsewhere","Ulster custom"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/custom#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:8bd9efb3fda1c46143","definition":"A custom (made-to-order) piece of art, etc.","example":"The rest of the necklace holders finally came in! If you bought a custom from me thank you so much for your patience! I’m gonna try my best to crank them out as fast as possible","pos":"noun","synonyms":["fashion","folkway","habit","practice","usage","wone","wont"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["custom and practice","custom-built","custom house","customless","grow a custom","heir by custom","suit custom","take one's custom elsewhere","Ulster custom"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/custom#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:de285f285dee7a7f6f","definition":"Familiar acquaintance; familiarity.","example":"Age can not wither her, nor custom stale\nHer infinite variety.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["fashion","folkway","habit","practice","usage","wone","wont"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"obsolete","register":"countable, obsolete, uncountable","wordFamily":["custom and practice","custom-built","custom house","customless","grow a custom","heir by custom","suit custom","take one's custom elsewhere","Ulster custom"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/custom#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:ecd1ab444f6f8bc815","definition":"Toll, tax, or tribute.","example":"Render therefore to all their dues: tribute to whom tribute is due; custom to whom custom; fear to whom fear; honour to whom honour.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["fashion","folkway","habit","practice","usage","wone","wont"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"archaic","register":"archaic, uncountable","wordFamily":["custom and practice","custom-built","custom house","customless","grow a custom","heir by custom","suit custom","take one's custom elsewhere","Ulster custom"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/custom#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:a9fb149d09f5d21254","definition":"Made or done in a way adjusted to fit the needs of a particular person or group (e.g., customer, health care patient, do-it-yourselfer), and thus specialized and, in some cases, unique.","example":"Near-synonyms: custom-made, tailored, tailor-made, custom-built, purpose-built; see also Thesaurus:custom-made","pos":"adj","synonyms":["bespoke","custom-made","tailored","tailor-made","custom-built","purpose-built","custom-made","made-to-measure","made-to-order","tailor-made"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"not-comparable","register":"not-comparable","wordFamily":["custom and practice","custom-built","custom house","customless","grow a custom","heir by custom","suit custom","take one's custom elsewhere